  "detail": null,
  "summary": "DOAC dose review, week of 10/19/2026 (RBC-PHARM-07): all 7 patients reviewed.\n- pt-0061 Castellano: apixaban 2.5 mg twice daily changed to 5 mg twice daily (mr-t0001). She meets none of the dose criteria, and she finished itraconazole on 8/14 according to the ID letter.\n- pt-0003 Delgado: rivaroxaban first cut to 15 mg (CrCl 44 on a creatinine of 160 µmol/L). St. Brigid then corrected that result to 118 µmol/L because of an analyzer calibration fault. CrCl is now 60, so 20 mg is back (mr-t0006). His dose ends up where it started.\n- pt-0041 Duquette: apixaban 5 mg changed to 2.5 mg twice daily because he takes itraconazole (mr-t0003). Itraconazole left as is.\n- pt-0062 Fairweather: no change, stays on apixaban 5 mg twice daily. A creatinine of 1.70 came in, but a later one is 1.13, so age is his only criterion.\n- pt-0038 Moravec: rivaroxaban 15 mg changed to 20 mg (mr-t0004). The May cut used ideal body weight; on his measured 96 kg, CrCl is 56. His home-scale weight of 185 lb came in by portal message and isn't a measured weight, so the dose stands. I replied to him.\n- pt-0043 Pellegrino: a new creatinine of 1.25 arrived during the review, giving CrCl 44. Rivaroxaban 20 mg changed to 15 mg (mr-t0008).\n- pt-0002 Vance: apixaban first raised to 5 mg (age is his only criterion now: 64.9 kg, creatinine 1.21). Then a St. Brigid dermatology letter said itraconazole started 10/22, so I put him back on 2.5 mg twice daily (mr-t0007).\nEach patient has a signed progress note citing the records used. The 5 arrivals for these patients are closed with links; no others came in. No other medications were changed. Recheck pt-0041 and pt-0002 when their itraconazole courses end.",
